B=(18, 8);
C=(24, 0);
D=(0,0);
O=(12,0);
P=(12,8);
X=(A+D)/2;
Y=(B+C)/2;
draw(X--Y, dashed);
draw(A--B--C--D--A);
draw(A--O--B);
draw(circumcircle(A,X,O),dashed);
draw(A--P, dashed);
label("A", A, NW);
label("B", B, NE);
label("C", C, SE);
label("D", D, SW);
label("O", O, S);
label("P", P, N);
label("X", X, NW);
label("Y", Y, NE);
label("h", (A+P)/2, E);
label("1", (X+P)/2, S);
label("3", (A+X)/2, N);[/asy] $h = \sqrt{12^2 - 3^2} = 3\sqrt{15}$.  The area of $\triangle AXO$ (and of quadrilateral $AXPY$) is $\dfrac{3\cdot 3\sqrt{15}}{2} = \dfrac{9\sqrt{15}}{2}$, since the side of the triangle corresponding to the altitude is $3$, and the area of triangle $AXO$ itself is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot h \cdot 3 = \dfrac{9\sqrt{15}}{2}$.  The total area of $ABYX$ is then $\dfrac{9\sqrt{15}}{2}+6\sqrt{15} = \dfrac{21\sqrt{15}}{2}$.  Since the total area of trapezoid $ABCD$ is $120$, then the area of $XYCD$ is $120 - \dfrac{21\sqrt{15}}{2}$.  The ratio of these areas is[asy]
